        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Apply [F3] to $p_t=p_0\\circ\\phi_{-t}$. It preserves $\\int p_t\\,dm=\\int p_0\\,dm=1$. The scalar function $u\\mapsto u\\log u$, defined to be $0$ at $u=0$ by [A3], is Borel; its absolute integrability is preserved because the same measure-preserving substitution gives $$\\int_R|p_t\\log p_t|\\,dm=\\int_R|p_0\\log p_0|\\,dm<\\infty.$$ Applying integral invariance to its positive and negative parts proves $\\int_Rp_t\\log p_t\\,dm=\\int_Rp_0\\log p_0\\,dm$, hence the stated fine-grained entropy conservation.",
          "step": "2.1",
