      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-12",
        "notes": "Checked all eight steps and all five supplier interfaces. Graph is closed/bounded; affine dependence removes atoms in finite iterations, giving compact conv(graph). Fiber is nonempty and compact. Finite Borel partitions approximate every integral, so minimization over arbitrary measures equals the graph-fiber minimum. Liminf pairs converge by construction; convexity uses combined minimizers; optimal-energy affine dependence reduces support from d+2 to d+1. Finite Jensen gives the greatest convex minorant. Nonempty K and d>=1 are explicit; only finite choices used. Reader replacement of sequential compactness is sound."
      }
