        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-12",
        "notes": "Read all ten steps and all original thirteen plus three added direct supplier interfaces. Deterministic Ito approximants and common continuous-event extension prove the integral equation without stochastic Fubini; split increments remain independent of F_s and give transition/moment laws. Pathwise uniqueness follows from integral inequality. Gaussian finite-dimensional laws and covariance prove stationarity; detailed balance exponent and Fokker-Planck derivatives checked. Gamma,sigma>0 ensure positive variance at t>s, with t=0 treated by a point mass. Confirmed refuter citation gap; exact modulus, entire derivative and componentwise FTC now prove the finite-R Fourier integral and its decay. Absolute E|XsXt|<=V justifies expectation/time Fubini for the time-average bound. Brownian/Ito AC convention inherited; no bath relation or empirical assertion.",
