        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-12",
        "notes": "Read every current coarea and invariance step and all direct supplier interfaces. IFT applies with a nonzero coordinate partial; finite chart partitions and Jacobian 1/|partial_i H| give nonnegative-Borel coarea, partition-independent weighted area, and positive finite mass on nonempty compact levels (n>=1). Confirmed smooth-only supplier mismatch: local step 1.2 now proves energy conservation and unit flow Jacobian using the C1 coordinate field for C2 H, its variational integral equation, determinant multilinearity and equality of continuous mixed second derivatives. Removed the smooth-only prerequisite, retained C2 Statement. Compact chart bounds give energy continuity, improving a.e. energy invariance to every regular energy; distance cutoffs and finite pi-system uniqueness extend continuous-test invariance to Borel sets. Empty shells excluded from normalization; critical/noncompact levels excluded. AC inherited for change of variables. ETH p70 C1 divergence-free proof independently checked as corroboration, not a replacement for local proof."
